{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdXkkTb4SBiKBczKRJYp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In the Nexus system at the Allen Telescope Array, a researcher can rewrite a signal-processing block by prompting in natural language. That capability sits next to others the article describes: agents can steer the antennae, calibrate and focus the instrument, catch and fix data errors and plot the result. Taken together, the agent's reach covers the hardware, the data and the code that analyzes the data.\n\nThe stack behind this has distinct parts. DAQIRI, a library in NVIDIA's Holoscan platform, pulls terabits per second of sensor data into GPU memory. CyberEther, a signal-processing framework developed at the SETI Institute, does the math using CUDA-X libraries including cuFFT and cuBLAS. Nexus, a web-based orchestrator, is the agent harness and gives agents a single source of truth for instrument state, compute resources and pipelines. The article says the system handles 2.4 terabits per second on NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell GPUs, with inference on premises, and that agents compress what would take humans weeks or years into hours. That timing claim comes from NVIDIA's own piece without a stated baseline.\n\nThe article is silent on how an agent's changes are checked. It says observations are processed in flight instead of filling hard drives, and it says agents catch and fix data errors, but it does not say whether raw data is kept for comparison or how a researcher confirms that a corrected stream or a rewritten processing block still reflects what the telescope received. For a search whose goal is to identify unusual signals, that verification step seems worth documenting as these agents take on more of the pipeline. The only result the article reports so far is the first real-time AI detection of a pulsar, in the Crab Nebula, a known object that a verification process could be tested against."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1019,"cache_read_input_tokens":5872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1019},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0856093-bf47-4a27-b619-fc92e43c6ae0","uuid":"635762f9-2add-4ac8-a579-b61535c16ca5","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:14:43.863Z","request_id":"req_011CgdXkkFgMvB6EvM9h573Z"}
